-- title:
--   Admissible rigidified modules arise from rigidified fake elliptic curves
-- statement:
--   Fix primes $r \neq \bar r$ and $N \neq 0$ with $r \nmid N$. Let $\mathcal O$ be a characteristic-zero domain which is a discrete valuation ring with irreducible element $\pi$, complete for the $\pi$-adic topology, with residue ring of cardinality $r$ and with $(r) = (\pi)$, and let $K_0$ be a characteristic-zero fraction field of $\mathcal O$. Let $Onr$ be a characteristic-zero domain over $\mathcal O$ carrying an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $Fr$, complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$, that ideal being maximal, such that every element of $Onr$ satisfies a monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo $\pi$, every monic polynomial over $Onr$ of positive degree has a root modulo $\pi$, and $Fr(x) \equiv x^{r} \pmod{\pi}$. Let $a, b \in \mathbb Q$ be such that $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q, a, b]$ satisfies `IsIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b r rbar`, i.e. $0 < a$ or $0 < b$ and, for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$, the completion $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b] \otimes_{\mathbb Q} \mathbb Q_v$ has all nonzero elements invertible exactly when $v$ contains $r$ or $\bar r$; let $\Lambda$ be a maximal order containing all rational integers, and $\mathrm{coord} : \Lambda \to \mathbb Z_{r}^{(2)} \times \mathbb Z_{r}^{(2)}$ an order coordinate in the sense of `IsOrderCoord` (additive, $1 \mapsto (1,0)$, multiplicative for the Frobenius-twisted product rule, injective, with dense image modulo each power of $r$, and matching reduced traces), where $\mathbb Z_r^{(2)}$ denotes the Witt vectors of the quadratic field of $r$ elements. Further data: a fake elliptic curve $A_0$ with $\Lambda$-action and level-$N$ structure over $Onr/\pi$, a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X_0$ of height $4$ over $Onr/\pi$ and $2$-dimensional formal coordinates $\theta_0$ for $A_0 \to \operatorname{Spec}(Onr/\pi)$ exhibiting $X_0$ as the formal module of $A_0$ via $\mathrm{coord}$; a ring map $\iota : \mathbb Z_r^{(2)} \to Onr$; a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $\Phi$ over $Onr/(r)$ which is special for the induced structure map and of height $4$; an injective ring map $E_0$ from the centraliser of the $\mathbb Z_r^{(2)}$-action and of $\varpi$ in $\operatorname{End}(\Phi)$ to $M_2(K_0)$ whose image is commensurable with $M_2(\mathcal O)$ (some $r^{m}M_2(\mathcal O)$ lies in the image and $r^{m}$ times the image lies in $M_2(\mathcal O)$); a ring map $\kappa : Onr/\pi \to Onr/(r)$ compatible with the quotient maps; and an isogeny $\beta_0$ from $\Phi$ to $X_0$ pushed along $\kappa$, of height $4n_0$. Finally let $k$ be an algebraically closed $\mathcal O$-algebra in which the images of $\pi$ and of $r$ are nilpotent, $\psi : Onr \to k$ an $\mathcal O$-algebra map, and $t = (X_t, n_t, \rho_t)$ a rigidified object over $k$ which is admissible for $(\iota, \psi)$, that is: $X_t$ is special for $\psi \circ \iota$ and of height $4$, and $\rho_t$ is an isogeny of height $4 n_t$ from the base change of $\Phi$ along $\psi$ to the reduction of $X_t$ modulo $r$. The assertion is that there exist a fake elliptic curve $E$ over $k$ together with a rigidification $\rho$ of $E$ relative to $A_0$ along $\psi$ (a pullback $E_b$ of $E$ to $k/\pi$, a pullback $A_b$ of $A_0$ along the residue leg, and a pair of mutually dual $r^{d}$-isogenies between $E_b$ and $A_b$ respecting the level structure), a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X$ over $k$, formal coordinates $\theta$ for $E$, and a rigidified object $t'$ over $k$, such that $\theta$ exhibits $X$ as the formal module of $E$ via $\mathrm{coord}$, $t'.X = X$, $t'$ is the rig-transport of $(\theta_0, \kappa, \beta_0, \rho, \theta)$ with twisting exponent $j = 0$ (so $t'.\rho$ is the composite of $\beta_0$ pushed to $k/(r)$ with the transported series, with no Frobenius twist $X_i \mapsto X_i^{r^{j}}$), $t'$ is again admissible for $(\iota, \psi)$, and $t'$ is isomorphic to $t$ as a rigidified object.
--
--   This is the algebraisation, or surjectivity, half of the Čerednik–Drinfeld comparison between rigidified fake elliptic curves over an algebraically closed base with $\pi$ and $r$ nilpotent and admissible rigidified special formal $\mathcal O_D$-modules: every such formal datum is realised, up to isomorphism, by a rigidified fake elliptic curve whose associated formal module is transported with trivial Frobenius twist. It is the input to [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.FakeEllipticCurve.rigidifiedToG_surjective_of_isAlgClosed`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.FakeEllipticCurve.rigidifiedToG_surjective_of_isAlgClosed).
